From 2255afd750de34f4efd4564e6feed6fe648a86ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Kush)" <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:31:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] remix api: adopt 0.16 C header, headless Startup on Linux

- public/include/remix/remix_c.h is the rtx-remix-minecraft 0.16.0 header
  with the native POSIX changes. Materials and dome lights take texture
  handles, resolved through an API texture registry (filled by
  CreateTextureFrom* later). The removed texture-transform fields use
  defaults.
- Every 0.16 entry point is registered. Unimplemented ones log once and
  return GENERAL_FAILURE. Config layers are accepted and ignored.
  GetConfigVariableResolved reads registered options.
- Linux Startup always uses the external swapchain and never creates a
  presenter or window surface. The frameEnd/frameResume handshake only
  runs once a client calls dxvk_GetExternalSwapchain.
- remixlinux_SetWindowSize export and REMIX_LINUX_WINDOW_SIZE fallback set
  the headless output size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb41TgDi74v7sgH5LJBZ5A
